# T line, T2 (2026-09-22): the CURRENT generation config (selected by current.argv).
# Same flag set as T1 fix7 -- T2 changes the data and the models, not the recipe:
#   library     scratch/txy_t2/release_aligned_k8_20260922   (+24 clips from 17 new uploads,
#               6112 train windows vs 5329; frozen k8 labels, same normalizer bytes 79a7867f)
#   planner     planner_aligned_k8_t2_sd20260901/planner_step4500.pt  (shipped argv, 300 epochs,
#               final checkpoint).  SEED CHOSEN ON VAL (2026-09-22): of the two seeds, 20260901
#               keeps the beat hitting of the T1 pipeline (val-30 settle_gain vs A0 -0.009, 12/29,
#               P=0.46; test-20 +0.013) while 20260902 loses it (val -0.064, 8/29, P=0.024) --
#               the planner seed moved this column as much as the library did.
#   completion  completion_txy_t2_seam4_sd20260902/completion_step57600.pt (shipped argv,
#               600 epochs, final checkpoint)
#   sidecars    scratch/txy_t2/sidecars_aligned_k8_20260922/  (regenerated from the T2 library:
#               name coverage alone cannot tell T1 files from T2 ones)
#   selector    unchanged (retrieval_selector_txy_t; no library index in it)
#   --floor-anchor 0.3391 = median per-clip floor over the 278 T2 train clips, the rule that
#               gave T1's 0.3396 over its 245 (re-measured: 0.3396)
#   --retrieval-max-yaw-step 25.2 / --retrieval-max-speed-spike 3.62 carried over unchanged
#   --ingest-root is the re-decoded audio overlay (T1 audio.wav is up to 161 ms early)
# infer_atomic refuses a planner/completion trained on a different release than --data-root
# was derived from (manifest "release_binding"), so this file cannot silently pair old and new.
#
# usage (from the repo root; per-invocation flags go AFTER the @file and win):
#   python3 infer_atomic.py @configs/t_line/current.argv --audio-dir <music npy dir> \
#       --sequence-list <list> --output-dir <new dir> [--dump-draft-dir <dir>]
